# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sidechain
#
# House rule: this repo holds code, configs and prose. Every byte of data,
# every checkpoint and every paper lives OUTSIDE it, under ~/data/sidechain/
# (see CLAUDE.md). The rules below are defence in depth -- the primary
# defence is simply not putting data here.
#
# To commit something these rules would hide (a small figure, a test fixture):
#   git add -f path/to/file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- python ----
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.eggs/

# ---- tooling ----
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- run output ----
# cell-eval writes results.csv / agg_results.csv / *_de.csv per run. Headline
# numbers are curated into RESULTS.md; the raw output is regenerable.
runs/
cell-eval-outdir/

# ---- single-cell / ML data ----
# The formats that actually bit us: an 18 GB h5ad and a 4 GB zip sat in this
# directory before the reorg.
*.h5ad
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.zarr/
*.loom
*.mtx
*.npz
*.npy
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
vcc_data/
.lamindb/

# ---- archives & papers (these belong in ~/data/sidechain/literature/) ----
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.pdf

# ---- machine-local ----
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
# Skills and slash commands describe the structure of the private docs they
# operate on, so they cannot live in the tracked part of .claude/. Note that
# .claude/settings.json is deliberately NOT ignored -- shared harness config is
# fine to publish; the procedures that read research/ are not.
.claude/skills/
.claude/commands/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- the private half of the project ----
# This repo is public. The working docs -- strategy, measurements, half-formed
# ideas, negative results -- are their own repo, checked out at private/ and
# hidden by this single rule. See private/README.md and CLAUDE.md.
#
# This used to be twelve separate rules, one per file. One rule is much harder
# to get wrong, and it fails safe: anything new dropped into private/ is hidden
# automatically instead of needing its own entry.
#
# Asymmetry worth remembering: publishing later is one commit; un-publishing
# later is a history rewrite plus a force-push. So the default is private.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore has no trailing comments -- `#` only starts a comment at the
# start of a line. `private/  # notes` matches a file literally named
# "private/  # notes", i.e. nothing. Keep every annotation on its own line.
private/
